          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01GujCfN8Yf3pJpN3CcaG3UQ",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/retrieval-patterns.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Retrieval Patterns\\ndescription: Techniques for combining and ranking results from multiple retrieval methods, especially hybrid retrieval combining lexical and semantic search.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Retrieval\\n  - concept/Ranking\\n  - concept/RAG\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Two sources; patterns are industry-standard but emerging documentation base.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\n## Hybrid Retrieval\\n\\nHybrid retrieval combines sparse lexical search (e.g., BM25) with dense vector search, then merges the two ranked result sets to capture both exact term matches and semantic similarity. This approach has become the default retrieval pattern in production RAG systems.\\n\\n### Mechanism\\n\\nThe pattern typically works as follows:\\n\\n1. **Sparse search**: Execute a lexical search (e.g., BM25) to find exact term matches and rare identifiers.\\n2. **Dense search**: Execute a vector search (semantic embedding similarity) to find semantically related content.\\n3. **Ranking and merging**: Merge the two result sets, often using reciprocal rank fusion, which weights the rankings from both methods to produce a single ranked result list.\\n\\n### Advantages\\n\\nHybrid retrieval consistently outperforms either method alone, especially on queries that mix:\\n- Rare identifiers (error codes, product SKUs, model numbers)\\n- Natural language intent and semantic meaning\\n\\nBy leveraging both exact matching and semantic understanding, it captures a broader range of relevant results than either approach in isolation.\\n\\n### Use Cases\\n\\nHybrid retrieval is particularly valuable in RAG systems where the retrieval step must handle diverse query types\\u2014from structured lookups to open-ended semantic questions.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Hybrid retrieval evaluation in production RAG systems (eval://update-over-duplicate/sample-02)\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
